sts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T07:40:43-07:00","id":895478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/892464-sons-of-urfarah?p=895410#post895410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Creator was Gurim? I thought that Gurim-Ur has always been crazy and because of that he was left alone to be forgotten.</div> </div> </div> </div>After checking Basra part, you're right they are different. The contradiction that the youngest Sagrim-Ur was presented at the birth of Skolis-Ur still remain though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11834-ben44","name":"Ben44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11834_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T08:26:31-07:00","id":895497,"title":"","content":"The stories of the Uratha are true - to those who tell them and those who listen. This does not necessarily make them concordant with one another, and such mutual exclusivity does not diminish their meaning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-21-2016, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T08:53:37-07:00","id":895508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/892464-sons-of-urfarah?p=895410#post895410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creator was Gurim? I thought that Gurim-Ur has always been crazy and because of that he was left alone to be forgotten.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pure offers a few suggestions for Gurim-Ur's origin, and one of them was as Danu-Ur. Some people use that origin, others don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T16:23:53-07:00","id":896374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/892464-sons-of-urfarah?p=895478#post895478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The contradiction that the youngest Sagrim-Ur was presented at the birth of Skolis-Ur still remain though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Zeus is the youngest of the six gods born to the Titans Rhea and Cronus, as the last god to be born from that union.<br /> <br /> Zeus is the oldest of the six gods born to the Titans Rhea and Cronus, as the one who has lived the longest outside the confines of his father's stomach.<br /> <br /> Both these stories are true. There is no contradiction, especially when it comes to mythological accounts and the Shadow's occasional adjustments to the passage of time and the Firstborn's existence as spiritual beings who can possess multiple discrete forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T19:13:18-07:00","id":934240,"title":"","content":"The exact identities of the Firstborn and their relationships to one another are intentionally obscure and the myths contradictory. That's how myths are. It's also not unusual for the same person to tell two mutually contradictory narratives. Tribal cultures have a great deal more tolerance for that sort of thing than folks in the Internet age, who want everything to line up in a strict, literal fashion. It's one of those things that highlights the culture clash between the People and their modern human herds.<br /> <br /> Also, the genders of the Firstborn are completely subjective, as spirits don't actually have sexes in the way animals do. I wouldn't be surprised if the First Tongue lacked grammatical gender entirely, making &quot;he&quot; and &quot;she&quot; a distinction that only comes through in translation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 07-19-2016, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}